      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Row 103, blue fescue. Care: NC State, Missouri BG and RHS agree on full sun, free drainage, drought tolerance and clumps that die out in the centre (divide every 2 to 3 years). Size 30 by 45 cm is the NC State and Missouri BG figure (23 to 30 cm tall, 30 to 45 cm spread); RHS only gives 10 to 50 cm. Hardiness H5 is the RHS rating (NC State zone 4 to 8, Missouri BG 4 to 8). Semi-evergreen per NC State and Missouri BG, so dormancy none. NC State and Missouri BG both say it declines in hot, humid summers. Growth rate not stated, left unknown. Toxicity: no page read states any and no ASPCA page was found, so people and pets are unknown. Es and it names are machine drafts. The Missouri BG Boulder Blue page was read for comparison and not cited as a source."
      },
